      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.1 Physical Geography"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Goa is geographically divided into three major natural zones: the Coastal Plains, the Intermediate Valley, and the Western Ghats (Sahyadris).",
        "Mandovi and Zuari are the two major estuarine rivers that form the backbone of Goa's drainage system and internal navigation.",
        "The Kalasa-Banduri Nala project is a major inter-state water dispute involving the Mahadayi (Mandovi) river diversion between Karnataka, Goa, and Maharashtra.",
        "Goa features 12 administrative talukas divided evenly between North Goa and South Goa districts.",
        "The Western Ghats region of Goa is a recognized biodiversity hotspot featuring protected areas like Bhagwan Mahaveer Sanctuary and Mollem National Park."
      ],
      "id": "qbvik24"
    },
